From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 21:45:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: tell the driver when decap offload turns off

ieee80211_check_fast_rx() clears WLAN_STA_DECAP_OFFLOAD when the
interface no longer allows decap offload, for example after a monitor
interface is added. It then reports the change to the driver with the
fast rx state instead of the offload state. For a station that can
still use fast rx, the driver keeps decap offload on, although the
interface does not allow it any more.

Pass the new state of WLAN_STA_DECAP_OFFLOAD to the driver.

Fixes: 80a915ec4427 ("mac80211: add rx decapsulation offload support")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/mac80211/rx.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -4860,7 +4860,8 @@ void ieee80211_check_fast_rx(struct sta_
 		set_offload = test_and_clear_sta_flag(sta, WLAN_STA_DECAP_OFFLOAD);
 
 	if (set_offload)
-		drv_sta_set_decap_offload(local, sdata, &sta->sta, assign);
+		drv_sta_set_decap_offload(local, sdata, &sta->sta,
+					  assign && offload);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&sta->lock);
 	old = rcu_dereference_protected(sta->fast_rx, true);
